        "id": 1112784
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-08-05T05:06:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, absolutely agreed.  I won\u0027t be able to get rid of uart.c until the generic uart_buffering code is re-written to use the stream based version of the serial API.  And that can\u0027t happen until all cores have been updated to use stream based serial drivers.  In the mean time I am planning on gutting uart.c (probably once we have a DMA capable version of the stream driver) and replacing it with calls out to a stream based usart.  In the mean time we can use the stream based API to write our console multiplexer and work towards a unified serial driver interface over time.",
      "parentUuid": "3692db12_5f94cbf4",
      "revId": "027f392aa05bc6366d5cf5fccd7bc5defd54b9cb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
